# Trees excluded from the code index. They stay tracked in git; this file
# only stops the scanner from reading them, so git history keeps every
# committed record while search results point at source.

# Captured round records, gate output and command logs. Indexing them made
# captures tie with or outrank source in semantic search, find-callers and
# hotspot rank. Anchored to the repository root: a directory of the same
# name below it (src/runs/ in a real project) is source, not a capture tree.
/runs/

# The retrieval evaluation corpus: one query per line with its labelled
# answers. Those lines are questions shaped like the ones users type, so
# indexing them ranks near-duplicate queries above the code they point at.
# The harness reads the file from disk, not from the index. Anchored to the
# repository root for the same reason as /runs/ above.
/eval/
